  "review_notes": "[v2] Compared the preview with all items. Running header (was a text item) omitted. Equations (7)-(14) converted from formula images / glyph text to LaTeX from the authors' TeX with macros expanded (\\Var, \\Cov -> \\mathrm{Var}, \\mathrm{Cov}; \\coloneqq -> ':='), \\cref resolved to the printed 'eq. (6)', 'eq. (8)'; every formula and its printed number checked against the page; (9) and (10), printed as one aligned group, are two $$ blocks so both tags stay visible. The paragraph 'Here, we want ...' and the next paragraph 'Importance sampling with MCMC ...' were one extracted item and are split as printed. Replacement characters removed from 'and $\\mu := \\mathrm{E}_p(f(x))$ as defined earlier.' Section heading '## 3. ...'. Authors' wording kept ('the following approximate of'). Page ends with display (14); page 5 starts a new sentence.",
  "warnings": [],
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "p0004-r00",
      "kind": "omit",
      "bbox": [
        110.0,
        76.0,
        503.0,
        82.0
      ],
      "markdown": "",
      "reason": "Running header (short title \"ITERATIVE IMPORTANCE SAMPLING WITH MARKOV CHAIN MONTE CARLO SAMPLING\") with page number 4; page furniture."
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004-r01",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        110.0,
        97.0,
        539.0,
        118.0
      ],
      "markdown": "The effective sample size represents the number of standard Monte Carlo samples that are needed for both estimators to have the same variance."
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004-r02",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        122.0,
        121.0,
        406.0,
        131.0
      ],
      "markdown": "If the samples $X_i$ from $q$ are i.i.d. then $\\mathrm{ESS}$ can be estimated by"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004-r03",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        105.0,
        134.0,
        539.0,
        174.0
      ],
      "markdown": "$$\n\\mathrm{ESS_{IS}} := \\frac{(\\sum_{i=1}^N w_p(X_i))^2}{\\sum_{i=1}^N w^2_p(X_i)}, \\tag{7}\n$$"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004-r04",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        110.0,
        177.0,
        539.0,
        199.0
      ],
      "markdown": "see [33]. However, this formula is not applicable for correlated samples, as would be the case if the $X_i$ are sampled from $q$ using an MCMC algorithm."
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004-r05",
      "kind": "heading",
      "bbox": [
        166.0,
        219.0,
        483.0,
        228.0
      ],
      "markdown": "## 3. Effective sample size of importance sampling using MCMC"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004-r06",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        110.0,
        237.0,
        539.0,
        260.0
      ],
      "markdown": "Here, we want to derive an estimate of the effective sample size as defined in eq. (6) when the $X_i$ are sampled from $q$ through MCMC. First, we derive an approximation of $\\mathrm{Var}_q(\\widetilde{\\mu})$."
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004-r07",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        110.0,
        261.0,
        539.0,
        284.0
      ],
      "markdown": "Importance sampling with MCMC was introduced by [21] for variance reduction [5]. Hastings [21] suggested the following approximate of the denominator in eq. (6):"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004-r08",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        105.0,
        287.0,
        539.0,
        332.0
      ],
      "markdown": "$$\n\\mathrm{Var}_q \\left(\\widetilde{\\mu}\\right) = \\mathrm{Var}_q\\left( \\frac{\\overline{Y}}{\\overline{Z}} \\right) \\approx \\frac{\\mathrm{Var}_q(\\overline{Y}-\\mu\\overline{Z})}{\\Bigl(\\mathrm{E}_q(\\overline{Z})\\Bigr)^2}, \\tag{8}\n$$"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004-r09",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        110.0,
        334.0,
        136.0,
        342.0
      ],
      "markdown": "where"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004-r10",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        105.0,
        346.0,
        539.0,
        383.0
      ],
      "markdown": "$$\n\\overline{Y} := \\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{i=1}^N f(X_i)w_p(X_i), \\tag{9}\n$$"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004-r11",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        105.0,
        384.0,
        539.0,
        421.0
      ],
      "markdown": "$$\n\\overline{Z} := \\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{i=1}^N w_p(X_i), \\tag{10}\n$$"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004-r12",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        110.0,
        424.0,
        274.0,
        443.0
      ],
      "markdown": "and $\\mu := \\mathrm{E}_p\\Bigl(f(x)\\Bigr)$ as defined earlier."
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004-r13",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        122.0,
        443.0,
        381.0,
        454.0
      ],
      "markdown": "First, let us evaluate the denominator in eq. (8). Note that"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004-r14",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        105.0,
        457.0,
        539.0,
        491.0
      ],
      "markdown": "$$\n\\mathrm{E}_q\\Bigl(w_p(X_i)\\Bigr) = \\int w_p(x)q(x)dx = \\int \\frac{c p(x)}{q(x)}q(x)dx = c, \\tag{11}\n$$"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004-r15",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        110.0,
        495.0,
        371.0,
        507.0
      ],
      "markdown": "so $\\mathrm{E}_q(\\overline{Z})=c$, and we can approximate the denominator via"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004-r16",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        105.0,
        509.0,
        539.0,
        553.0
      ],
      "markdown": "$$\n\\Bigl(\\mathrm{E}_q(\\overline{Z})\\Bigr)^2 \\approx \\left(\\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{i=1}^N w_p(X_i)\\right)^2. \\tag{12}\n$$"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004-r17",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        110.0,
        556.0,
        304.0,
        567.0
      ],
      "markdown": "The numerator in eq. (8) is more tricky. Let"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004-r18",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        110.0,
        575.0,
        539.0,
        587.0
      ],
      "markdown": "$$\ng(X_i) := (f(X_i)-\\mu) w_p(X_i). \\tag{13}\n$$"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004-r19",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        110.0,
        596.0,
        226.0,
        606.0
      ],
      "markdown": "With this notation, we get"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0004-r20",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        105.0,
        608.0,
        539.0,
        655.0
      ],
      "markdown": "$$\n\\mathrm{Var}_q(\\overline{Y}-\\mu\\overline{Z}) = \\frac{1}{N^2} \\left( \\sum_{i = 1}^N \\mathrm{Var}_q\\Bigl(g(X_i)\\Bigr) + 2 \\sum_{i < j} \\mathrm{Cov}_q \\Bigl(g(X_i), g(X_j) \\Bigr) \\right). \\tag{14}\n$$"
    }
  ]
}